# promise: #825
# View ▸ Zoom to Actual Size (⌘0) puts the page back to its actual size after a trackpad pinch too, as Arc and Chrome
# do (Chrome's reset sets the zoom level and the page scale). Cra's set only the zoom level, so a pinched page stayed
# magnified (GitHub #825, joodaloop, 0.1.56). The pinch is the page scale a trackpad pinch sets, through the page's
# DevTools session; the reset is the menu's own action, after a pinch alone and after a pinch with ⌘+ on top.
budget rss=600 stalls50=6
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true}
pace 0.5
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=pinch
wait 3
cra://debug?pageScale=2
wait 1
cra://debug?pageScale=read:pinched
expect-log page scale pinched: 2\.00 zoom level: 0
cra://action/resetZoom
wait 1
cra://debug?pageScale=read:reset
expect-log page scale reset: 1\.00 zoom level: 0
cra://debug?pageScale=3
cra://action/zoomIn
wait 1
cra://debug?pageScale=read:both
expect-log page scale both: [0-9.]+ zoom level: 0\.5
cra://action/resetZoom
wait 1
cra://debug?pageScale=read:both-reset
expect-log page scale both-reset: 1\.00 zoom level: 0
